REASONING: The dilation centered at the origin with scale factor $-3$ can be represented by multiplying any vector $(x, y)$ by $-3$. This results in the new coordinates $( -3x, -3y )$. Therefore, the matrix corresponding to this transformation is:

$$
\begin{bmatrix}
-3 & 0 \\
0 & -3
\end{bmatrix}
$$

ANSWER: $$
\begin{bmatrix}
-3 & 0 \\
0 & -3
\end{bmatrix}
$$
